1. What you may do
  a. Play: download the official releases, install them and play them on
     your own devices, and record, stream and share videos and screenshots
     of the game (monetized or not), as long as you do not present the
     Software as made by anyone other than the Owner.
  b. Make content: create mods, charts, songs, scripts, characters, stages and
     other content that runs in the Software, and share it however you like.
     Your content is yours, as long as it does not contain the Software's
     code.
  c. Read the source code in the official repository. You may build it on
     your own devices for your own use, and try changes there in private to
     describe them in an issue, but you may not share the code, your changes
     or what you build.

2. What you may not do
  Unless the Owner has given written permission (section 4), you may not:
  a. fork the official repository, or copy the Software or any part of its
     code to any other place (another repository, a website, a file host, a
     mod, another game or engine);
  b. publish, share or distribute the Software, a modified version of it or
     builds of either, other than the official releases;
  c. publish the Software, a modified version of it, or a program built from
     its code as another project or engine, under any name;
  d. use the Software's code, or any part of it, in another program;
  e. remove or change the copyright notice, this License or the credits,
     present the Software or any part of it as your own work, or name
     yourself as its author or co-author;
  f. sell the Software or a modified version of it, or charge for access to
     either;
  g. use the names "God's Hand of Principality and Demise" or "God's Hand"
     for another project.
  These apply to every version, the old ones included (see "Every version").

  About forks: GitHub's Terms of Service let any GitHub user press "Fork" on
  a public repository, and this License cannot take that button away. A fork
  made that way gives no permission at all: it may not be changed, built,
  run, published or used in any other way, and it must be deleted when the
  Owner asks.

3. Contributing: only through issues
  The ONLY way to contribute to the Software is to open an issue in the
  official repository: report a bug, suggest a feature or an improvement, or
  explain an idea (short code snippets are welcome). Pull requests, patches
  and forks are not accepted. By writing in an issue you agree that the
  Owner may use what you suggest in the Software, under this License or any
  later license the Owner chooses; your issue stays in the repository's
  history with your name.

4. Written permission
  The Owner can give written permission for something section 2 forbids, in
  an issue of the official repository or in a file there. A permission
  covers only what it says, and the work must always credit the Software as
  "Based on God's Hand of Principality and Demise by deatuamae67-crypto",
  with a link to the official repository.

5. Mods and mod packs
  The mod packs published on the "mods" release are not part of the Software
  and are not covered by this License. Not all of them are the Owner's: some
  were made by the Owner, and the others belong to their original creators,
  who keep every right to them. They are shared so they can be played in
  God's Hand.

